plugin-hostd-protocol (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: plugin-hostd-protocol 0.7.0
  * ABI baseline carries types; release.yml header names the quick matrix
  * ci: turn the commit identity check on for pull requests
  * README: install instructions for Fedora 45 and Debian trixie arm64
  * CI: deb jobs on arm64 runners, Fedora 44 dropped
  * Drop the qualification_dir conf key, its subdirectory constant and its
    environment default
  * Reply shapes: plan, plan_get and estimate require every word of their one
    reply form
  * spec: the plugin-db-contract comment says what the floor is for
  * deps: keep the plugin-db-contract floor at 0.4.4, 0.4.7 is not served to
    fc44 and trixie yet
  * render: the plugin-db words come from plugin-db 0.4.7, whose address
    formats live in its domain document
  * commit-msg hook: follow the shared stub again, drop its arm of
    no-backcompat (#109)
  * commit-msg hook: read the OPENMIXER_* settings only, drop the deprecated
    FREEMIXER_* names (#109)
  * Tests: remove macro_compat, a build-compatibility check for older X-macro
    shapes (#109)
  * Packages: no relation to plugin-hostd-contract, the package this one
    replaced (#109)
  * Host errors: one name each, no ERR_LV2_* alias of the ERR_HOST_* codes
    (#109)
  * Reply forms: one per verb, no short form of an older daemon's reply (#109)
  * protocol.h: the qualify spool and event macros carry their doxygen
    comments
  * tests: the table-constants check joins verb_table.py (test audit row 6)
  * protocol: qualify_requested and the qualify spool, declared before the
    daemon writes them
  * ci: the TypeScript codec step takes the node the build dependencies
    already installed
  * ts codec: the library reads no environment, the contract floor has no
    ceiling, CI holds the reasons and the sentences
  * ts: the table-driven codec of plugin-hostd's TypeScript client is this
    package's `.` export

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:54:40 +0000
